# Optional: publish the Wildfire Watch finder without a login.
#
# Off by default. To turn it on, paste the block below into deploy/Caddyfile,
# inside the site block and above the `handle` that asks for the login, then
# `docker compose -f deploy/compose.hosted.yaml restart caddy`.
#
# Before you do, read RUNBOOK.md section 5b. In short:
#   - The finder works without a login, but place search and fire weather need
#     one, so anonymous readers get the list, the filters and the location view.
#   - Every anonymous reader arrives from Caddy's address, so they share the
#     same rate-limit bucket as logged-in users; cached answers are not counted.
#   - The location view embeds ALERTCalifornia camera frames; check their terms
#     before showing them to the public.
#
# Exactly these paths and nothing else: every other /api route can spend a
# provider key.

	@publicFireList path /wildfire /wildfire/ /wildfire/app.js /wildfire/finder.js /api/fire-risk
	handle @publicFireList {
		reverse_proxy {$APP_UPSTREAM} {
			header_up Host {host}
			header_up X-Real-IP {remote_host}
		}
	}
